  "review_decisions": [
    "Separate the characteristic inverse, compact-support modification and oscillatory defect estimate.",
    "A zero integrated auxiliary mean removes only the defect mean unless the source is auxiliary independent.",
    "The large drift is held fixed under coefficient differentiation; finite regularity gives only finitely many inverse powers.",
    "Generalize shrinking-cutoff summation to increasing decay orders; retain the existing Borel jet theorem as the normal-derivative special case.",
    "Separate the finite polynomial difference estimate from flat-residual realization.",
    "The residual proof fixes one sufficiently late stage; it does not sum stagewise flat errors.",
    "Cut off vector potentials before taking curl; directly cut off only divergence-free fields tangent to the scale levels.",
    "Keep finite input derivative requirements distinct from uniform losses in powers of the small scale.",
    "Use the exact quadratic residual after each fixed-inverse update.",
    "Endpoint extension requires compatible limits of all derivatives, obtained from bounds one time derivative higher.",
    "Move the generic shrinking-cutoff alias from the Borel jet special case to the new general summation owner.",
    "Give ordinary recursive sequence construction a foundational owner and complete the existing maximum prerequisite."
  ],
